# Root-level ignores. frontend/ and backend/ each have their own .gitignore too.

# Product photos are large binaries that land here as a staging area — they
# get uploaded to S3 via the admin panel, not committed to the repo (same
# reasoning as not committing node_modules).
product-images/*
!product-images/README.md

# Hero/marketing banner images (not per-SKU product shots) — same reasoning.
banners/*
!banners/README.md

# Same staging-area reasoning, but this one lives inside frontend/public and
# got accidentally committed (271 raw, unoptimized files, ~500MB, half of it
# exact duplicates) — see frontend/public/images/products/README.md, which
# already documented "not committed to git" as the intent.
frontend/public/images/products/*
!frontend/public/images/products/README.md

# A second, complete copy of product-images/categories/ (~230MB, byte-for-byte
# identical) had also been committed here by mistake. Never let anything land
# in frontend/public/product-images/ — anything under frontend/public/ is
# copied verbatim into every Vite build, so this alone made every `vercel
# deploy` upload ~1GB. Use the root-level product-images/ staging area instead.
frontend/public/product-images/
